#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""La poule (story 104, cycle 55; a hook, a literal clause met, an escalation through the whole country, a reversal, a dry last line).
This man loses a tooth biting an apple from his own tree; his insurer refuses: « when hens have teeth ». The next day his hen has one tooth: refused,
« teeth » is plural. The day after she has two, an expert finds them real and the insurer pays. The whole country brings out its old promises made on the
same condition: he gets his raise, and the minister has to keep the retirement at fifty he promised. The whole country retires, the minister first. The
retired feed the hen grain, but with teeth she prefers steak. An inspector gets bitten and the insurer refuses: « hens have no teeth ». Then his dentist
recognises his own work on a plaster mould: they were his teeth, left one by one in his apples and pecked up by the hen. Teeth found: nothing to pay back,
and the retirement is cancelled too. New clause: « when pigs fly ». He buys a pig. And two plane tickets.
Running gag (the tooth transfer, counted on the apples, never on his mouth): every apple he bites keeps one big white tooth (poApple: a bite face and a
tooth stuck in it), the heap of bitten apples grows in step with the hen's grin (S02 one apple, S04 two then three, S10 and S13 a heap with one gold tooth);
the hen's teeth are oversized white blocks on her lower beak (poHen: one alone in S02, two in S04-S05, a full set with one gold in S10-S13), always shot
at hen height; the gold tooth sparkles on the hen and on the apple heap, and the plaster mould of his teeth (poMould, S12) matches her grin, gold tooth in
the same place. His mouth is shown twice only: one black gap in S01b, no teeth at all in S13 (poGrin over his painted mouth); everywhere else it is closed.
The clause comes back three times by ear: met (S02-S05b), turned against a victim (S11b, the inspector's form slapped back), replaced (S15, the flying pig
poster); the last shot beats it with the same literal logic (a pig in a plane window seat, two boarding cards).
Staging: S01 under his apple tree, waist up and low: he bites a big red apple, tugs, his neck stretches after it, the tooth pops out with the apple (twang),
he stares at the tooth in the bite, a double take. S01b his grin at the lens: one black gap. S01c the insurer's counter (MUTUELLE): he holds up the
apple three-quarters to us, all hope; the clerk pushes his form back and speaks the clause with a smug « never » (finger up, eyes shut, a slow head
shake); his hope drains and his jaw drops as a block. S02 morning by the henhouse at
hen height: the hen pecks the bitten apple, turns to the lens and grins on « dent »: one big tooth, a sparkle. S03 the clerk lifts a big stamp, it
trembles, slams; the form springs up to the lens with a red cross; two hard finger-taps with a head bob each, a smug tilt (PLURIEL). S04 hen height: his mitten dangles and drops a third bitten apple on the heap
(on a low crate, above the captions); the hen follows it, turns to us and clacks her beak open, shut, open on « deux »: a sparkle on each tooth. S05 an expert in a head mirror kneels at her open beak with a big dental mirror, the head mirror
glints, two grave nods. S05b the clerk, sour, pushes a big blank cheque at us, hangs on to it (rubber arm) and lets go. S06 a terrace of five pastel
houses seen along the row from a low camera, the nearest neighbour large: the doors bang open flat against the wall in a cascade, five neighbours step
out with big yellowed envelopes, breathe in and blow a big cloud of dust off them. S06b the
nearest pulls out her letter: a drawing of a hen with teeth. S07 the office: the grim boss pushes a fat envelope across the desk, a tug of war with
his rubber arm stretched, lets go (his arm snaps back); the hero snaps back with a closed-mouth smile. S08 a plain official room (no flag): on the minister's lectern a framed photo of him smiling on
a deckchair; he glances at it, double take, gulps, a sweat drop. S09 an open-plan office: five employees spring up together and lift folded deckchairs
(RETRAITE). S09b seen from the corridor: the minister dashes out of the door first, deckchair and fishing rod, the five file out behind. S10 the
garden at hen height: three retirees in sunhats on deckchairs pour grain; the hen grins (full set, gold tooth sparkling), looks at the grain and turns
her head away. S10b she tears into a T-bone steak, big chewing bites, the retirees stare (one jaw drop). S11 an inspector in grey bends over her to
count her teeth with his clipboard: snap on his mitten, he leaps up, hangs in the air, drops flat as a pancake and pops back (unhurt). S11b the counter
again, the other way round: he blows on his throbbing mitten (stars), the clerk flicks his form onto his chest (a wince) and holds up a drawing of a
toothless hen as she speaks the clause. S12 his dentist (big round glasses) kneels beside her and holds the plaster mould
up beside her open beak: the same grin, the gold tooth in the same place, both sparkle; she looks from the mould to him; he turns his head toward the hero. S13 hen height: the hero
kneels beside her (she stands on a crate), both grin at the lens: his mouth toothless, hers full; they blink together. S14 the lobby: the retirees file
back in with their folded deckchairs, glum, the minister last with his rod. S14b he lays his framed photo face down on the reception desk (a soft dust puff)
and sinks into his shoulders, his fishing rod drooping. S15 the clerk
unrolls and pins a poster of a pig with wings behind her, turns, slaps her arms into a fold, a slow smug tilt, speaks the new clause. S16 a plane cabin: a big pink pig with
little white costume wings buckled in the window seat, clouds sliding past; it turns to us and flutters its wings. S16b wider: the pig (whole head and a wing), the
window, the hero holding up two big blank boarding cards, mouth closed; the pig wiggles on « deux billets »; hold.
Natural look; cycle 55: props_poule.js (poHen, poApple, poWholeApple, poApplePile, poAppleTree, poCoop, poGrin, poMould, poPhoto, poOldLetter, poForm,
poCheque, poPoster, poCounter, poSteak, poGrain, poScoop, poHeadMirror, poDentalMirror, poFoldedChair, poFishingRod, poRowHouses, poRoom, poWall,
poCrate, poReception, poCabin, poPig, poCards, poSparkle, poFill, poNoShadow, poPuff, poHenCard, poThrob); reused: bigStamp (props_eternuement), plEnvelope and plSunHat
(props_pelle), deckChair (props_soleil), grinLectern (props_grincement), clipBoard (props_bus), impactStars (props_interrupteur), sweatDrop, glasses,
desk, chair, fence, cottage (props.js); sets grassland, office, whiteVoid.
Lessons applied from the start: Looney deformation on every gag accent (the neck stretched after the apple and the snap, the double take, the hen's
squash and stretch on each grin, the stamp's trembling hold and slam, the rubber-arm cheque and envelope, the doors' cascade, the springing employees,
the minister's dash, the hen's head flick, the inspector's leap, the clerk's flick and the slap); every action starts in the first 0.3 s of its shot;
the hero's reactions framed with nobody in front; look targets at head height or 'camera'; blinks and breathing on holds; word timings from
timeline.json through st.at (words from 0, printed beside their times); every cut set just under its frame; cameras checked with project() (CHECKS);
soft blob shadows off with castShadow and receiveShadow (poNoShadow); flat floor props with a polygon offset; carried and passed objects are one world
prop each (apples, form, stamp, cheque, envelopes, mould, photo, cards); distinct models for the clerk, the expert, the dentist, the boss, the minister,
the inspector; new props prefixed po; sound names checked against audio3.py/audio.py/mix.py; no raised arm held still; no flag, emblem, organisation or
brand (a plain MUTUELLE sign, a plain umbrella picture); a framed holiday photo, no poster; no digits or currency on screen; French only; nobody hurt."""
from story_kit import *
import math

st = Story('poule', look='natural')
st.plan([('S01', 'L01', 0), ('S01b', 'L01', 5), ('S01c', 'L01', 6), ('S02', 'L02', 0), ('S03', 'L03', 0), ('S04', 'L04', 0), ('S05', 'L05', 0), ('S05b', 'L05', 4),
         ('S06', 'L06', 0), ('S06b', 'L06', 7), ('S07', 'L07', 0), ('S08', 'L08', 0), ('S09', 'L09', 0), ('S09b', 'L09', 7), ('S10', 'L10', 0), ('S10b', 'L10', 7),
         ('S11', 'L11', 0), ('S11b', 'L11', 5), ('S12', 'L12', 0), ('S13', 'L13', 0), ('S14', 'L14', 0), ('S14b', 'L14', 4), ('S15', 'L15', 0), ('S16', 'L16', 0), ('S16b', 'L16', 6)])
# (cycle 55, story_kit rounding) every cut just under its frame: 242/30 rounded to 8.0667 falls after the frame and its first image shows the last shot
st.SH = {sid: (math.floor(a * 10000 + 1e-6) / 10000, math.floor(b * 10000 + 1e-6) / 10000 if b < st.total else b) for sid, (a, b) in st.SH.items()}

PI = math.pi
def r(v, n=3): return round(v, n)
def add(a, b): return [r(a[i] + b[i]) for i in range(3)]
def lerp3(a, b, u): return [r(a[i] + (b[i] - a[i]) * u) for i in range(3)]
def yaw(src, dst): return r(math.degrees(math.atan2(dst[0] - src[0], dst[2] - src[2])), 1)
def fwd(ry): return [math.sin(math.radians(ry)), 0.0, math.cos(math.radians(ry))]
def right(ry): return [-math.cos(math.radians(ry)), 0.0, math.sin(math.radians(ry))]
def off(p, ry, f=0.0, s=0.0, y=0.0): F, R = fwd(ry), right(ry); return [r(p[0] + F[0] * f + R[0] * s), r(p[1] + y), r(p[2] + F[2] * f + R[2] * s)]
CHECKS = []
def chk(sid, frm, look, lens, pts):
    CHECKS.append(f"{sid}: " + ' | '.join(f"{n} {project(frm, look, lens, p)}" for n, p in pts.items()))
def chkc(sid, c, pts, end=False):
    frm, look = (c.get('to') or c['from'], c.get('lookAt2') or c['lookAt']) if end else (c['from'], c['lookAt'])
    chk(sid + ('>' if end else ''), frm, look, c['lens'], pts)
def W(sid, lid, i):
    # (cycle 51) word timings from timeline.json: st.at counts the words from 0; the word is printed beside its time
    t = st.at(sid, lid, i); CHECKS.append(f"{sid} « {st.L[lid]['words'][i]['w']} » at {t}"); return t
EZ = {'linear': lambda u: u, 'inOut': lambda u: 2 * u * u if u < 0.5 else 1 - (-2 * u + 2) ** 2 / 2, 'out': lambda u: 1 - (1 - u) ** 3, 'in': lambda u: u ** 3}
def track(p0, moves):
    # where a prop moved by `to` keys is at t (each move starts where the last one ended; eases as the engine's): hands follow it exactly
    def at_(t):
        p = list(p0)
        for t0, to, d, e in sorted(moves, key=lambda m: m[0]):
            if t < t0: break
            u = EZ[e](1.0 if d <= 0 else min(1.0, (t - t0) / d)); p = [p[i] + (to[i] - p[i]) * u for i in range(3)]
        return [r(v) for v in p]
    return at_
def MOVES(moves): return [k(t0, to=list(to), dur=d, ease=e) for t0, to, d, e in moves]
def FALL(t0, p0, p1, dur, n=4):
    # (cycle 51) a drop by gravity: linear `to` keys at the u^2 positions (an ease-in cubic puts the whole fall in the last frame)
    return [(r(t0 + dur * (i - 1) / n), lerp3(p0, p1, (i / n) ** 2), r(dur / n), 'linear') for i in range(1, n + 1)]

EX = {'holdLife': 2.5, 'shift': 2.4, 'breathe': 1.8}
def R5(p, w=1, s=0.04): return [*p, w, s]
def blink(t, face, keep=None): return [k(t, toon={**(keep or {}), 'face': {**face, 'lid': 1.0}}, toonDur=0.05), k(r(t + 0.1), toon={**(keep or {}), 'face': face}, toonDur=0.06)]
def life(t0, t1, face, keep=None, ph=0.0, blinks=(), period=0.9, amp=0.013):
    # a moving hold: slow breathing keys that carry the face and the hands (a toon key is a whole state), clear of the blinks
    out, bl, t_, i = [], sorted(blinks), t0 + ph, 0
    while t_ < t1 - 0.1:
        if not any(-0.04 < t_ - b < 0.2 for b in bl):
            q = [r(1 - amp * 0.4, 4), r(1 + amp, 4), r(1 - amp * 0.4, 4)] if i % 2 == 0 else [r(1 + amp * 0.3, 4), r(1 - amp * 0.6, 4), r(1 + amp * 0.3, 4)]
            out.append(k(r(t_), toon={**(keep or {}), 'sq': q, 'face': face}, toonDur=r(period * 0.8), toonEase='inOut'))
        t_ += period / 2; i += 1
    for b in bl: out += blink(r(b), face, keep)
    return out
def TALK(t0, t1, face, keep=None, step=0.1, shake=0.0, nod=0.05, tilt=0.0, pitch=0.0, blinks=()):
    # lip flaps for somebody who speaks the clause (never the hero): open / o / line shapes, small nods, a head shake if asked; tilt: the head kept
    # leaning to one side, pitch: the chin kept up (< 0); blinks: the lids shut on the keys that fall in those 0.1 s windows
    out, t_, i = [], t0, 0
    while t_ < t1 - 0.04:
        m = ['open', 'o', 'line', 'open', 'smirk'][i % 5]
        bd = {**(keep or {}).get('bend', {}), 'neck': [r(pitch + (nod if i % 3 == 0 else -nod * 0.5)), r(tilt + shake * math.sin(i * 1.9)), 0, 1, None]}
        lid = {'lid': 1.0} if any(0 <= t_ - b_ < 0.1 for b_ in blinks) else {}
        out.append(k(r(t_), toon={**(keep or {}), 'bend': bd, 'face': {**face, 'mouth': m, 'jaw': 0.25 if m in ('open', 'o') else 0.0, **lid}}, toonDur=r(step * 0.7)))
        t_ += step; i += 1
    return out
def HDT(t0, look_at, keep=None, back='camera', pop=0.45, blank=0.2, hold=0.32):
    # the hero's double take with his mouth shut (story_kit's doubleTake opens the jaw: his mouth is shown twice only)
    keep = dict(keep or {}); sn = r(t0 + 0.16 + blank); f0 = dict(keep.get('face', {}))
    return [k(t0, look=look_at, lookDur=0.12), k(r(t0 + 0.16), look=back, lookDur=0.12), k(sn, look=look_at, lookDur=0.06),
            k(r(sn - 0.04), toon={**keep, 'sq': [1.05, 0.94, 1.05]}, toonDur=0.03),
            k(sn, toon={**keep, 'sq': [0.93, 1.09, 0.93], 'hairUp': 0.8, 'face': {**f0, 'pop': pop, 'popLen': 0.22, 'brow': 1, 'mouth': 'line', 'jaw': 0.0}}, toonDur=0.04, toonEase='outBack'),
            k(r(sn + hold), toon={**keep, 'face': {**f0, 'brow': 0.7, 'mouth': 'line'}}, toonDur=0.12)]
def NOSHADOW(pid, who): return P(pid, 'poNoShadow', pos=[0, 0, 0], opts={'who': who})
def NEVER(t0, t1, face, keep_fn, amp=0.3, hz=0.8, step=0.067, pitch=-0.08):
    # the smug « never » while speaking: a slow head shake carried by dense keys (cycle 53: every 0.067 s, otherwise each key breaks the turn), the chin up,
    # lip flaps every 0.1 s; keep_fn(t) gives the hands at t (a toon key is a whole state)
    out, t_ = [], t0
    while t_ < t1 - 0.02:
        i = int((t_ - t0) / 0.1); m = ['open', 'o', 'line', 'open', 'smirk'][i % 5]; kp = keep_fn(t_)
        bd = {**kp.get('bend', {}), 'neck': [pitch, 0, r(amp * math.sin(2 * PI * hz * (t_ - t0))), 1, None]}
        out.append(k(r(t_), toon={**kp, 'bend': bd, 'face': {**face, 'mouth': m, 'jaw': 0.2 if m in ('open', 'o') else 0.0}}, toonDur=r(step * 0.9)))
        t_ += step
    return out

# ============================== the hero
HF = {'lid': 0.3, 'mouth': 'smile', 'brow': 0.2}
HAND = lambda R=None, L=None, hr='grip', hl='rest', **x: {'reach': {**({'R': R5(R, 1, 0.0)} if R else {}), **({'L': R5(L, 1, 0.0)} if L else {})}, 'hands': {'R': hr, 'L': hl}, 'hip': 0, **x}
# the hero's mouth overlay: shown twice (S01b the gap, S13 no teeth)
def GRIN(pid, kind, opn): return P(pid, 'poGrin', on={'actor': 'mec', 'joint': 'head', 'offset': [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]}, opts={'kind': kind, 'open': opn, 'y': 0.12, 'z': 0.1, 'w': 0.21, 'h': 0.105})

# ============================== the hen (a prop: pivot at her feet, front +Z, about 1.1 m tall); her beak and teeth at hen height
def HEN(pid, pos, ry, **o): return P(pid, 'poHen', pos=list(pos), ry=ry, opts=o)
def hen_head(pos, ry, s=1.0): return off(pos, ry, 0.44 * s, 0.0, 0.88 * s)
def hen_beak(pos, ry, s=1.0): return off(pos, ry, 0.55 * s, 0.0, 0.84 * s)
def CLUCK(sid, t, g=0.3): st.cue('sfx:cluck', sid, r(t), g)
GOLD = 1

# ============================== the garden (grassland, his house behind, an apple tree, the henhouse)
GSET = {'grass': '#86BE5C', 'clouds': 30}
TREE = [-1.25, 0.0, -1.9]; COOP = [1.75, 0.0, -2.05]
def GARDEN(n, tree=TREE, coop=COOP, coop_ry=-20, house=True):
    out = [P(f'arbre{n}', 'poAppleTree', pos=list(tree)), P(f'poulailler{n}', 'poCoop', pos=list(coop), ry=coop_ry),
           P(f'barriere{n}', 'fence', pos=[0.0, 0.0, -4.6], opts={'length': 16, 'height': 1.0, 'color': '#F6F4EE', 'rail': '#F6F4EE'})]
    if house: out.append(P(f'maison{n}', 'cottage', pos=[0.6, 0.0, -10.5], opts={'color': '#F2E3C8', 'roof': '#B5402F', 'door': '#2F7F8C'}))
    return out
LOOKG = {'sunDir': [0.35, 0.85, 0.75]}

# ============================== the insurer's counter (poCounter at the origin: counter front z 0, back wall z -1.6)
CSET = {'color': '#DCE8E2'}
CLF = {'lid': 0.45, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': 0.35}
def COUNTER(n, **o): return P(f'guichet{n}', 'poCounter', pos=[0, 0, 0], opts=o)
CTOP = 1.075

for g_ in [('S01', 0.85, 'mec', 'double take on the tooth'), ('S01b', 0.25, 'mec', 'gap grin'), ('S01c', 1.6, 'guichet', 'clause'), ('S03', 0.55, 'guichet', 'stamp slam'),
           ('S07', 1.05, 'mec', 'raise'), ('S08', 1.7, 'ministre', 'gulp'), ('S11', 1.1, 'controleur', 'bitten'), ('S12', 1.9, 'dentiste', 'recognises'), ('S13', 0.6, 'mec', 'toothless grin'),
           ('S15', 1.5, 'guichet', 'smug'), ('S16b', 1.0, 'mec', 'boarding cards')]:
    st.gag(*g_)

# 1: the hook. Under his apple tree, waist up and a little low: he already has a big red apple at his mouth and bites; he tugs it away, his neck
#    stretches after it (the head follows the apple), then the tooth lets go with a twang: the apple flies to arm's length, the head snaps back with a
#    squash; the bite turns to us with one big white tooth stuck in it; he stares at it, glances at us, double take (eyes out, mouth shut)
D1 = st.dur('S01'); DENT1 = W('S01', 'L01', 5)
H1 = [-0.25, 0.0, -0.55]
F1 = [0.62, 1.42, 1.85]; L1 = [-0.18, 1.62, -0.55]
RY1 = r(yaw(H1, F1) * 0.55, 1)
C1 = cam(0.0, F1, add(F1, [-0.05, 0.02, -0.18]), L1, add(L1, [0.0, 0.02, 0.0]), lens=40, ease='inOut')
MOUTH1 = off(H1, RY1, 0.3, 0.0, 1.76)
MID1 = off(H1, RY1, 0.42, -0.14, 1.66)
AWAY1 = off(H1, RY1, 0.5, -0.36, 1.52)
BITE1, TUG1, SNAP1 = 0.08, 0.16, 0.36
chkc('S01', C1, {'headTop': add(H1, [0, 2.35, 0]), 'chin': add(H1, [0, 1.62, 0]), 'mouthApple': MOUTH1, 'away': AWAY1, 'waist': add(H1, [0, 1.0, 0]), 'treeTop': add(TREE, [0, 3.3, 0])})
AM1 = [(TUG1, MID1, r(SNAP1 - TUG1), 'in'), (SNAP1, AWAY1, 0.06, 'out')]
AT1 = track(MOUTH1, AM1)
GRIP1 = lambda p: add(p, [0.0, -0.1, -0.02])
HERO1 = [k(0.0, look=add(MOUTH1, [0, 0.0, 0.2])), k(0.0, toon={**HAND(GRIP1(MOUTH1)), 'bend': {'neck': [0.18, 0, 0, 1, None]}, 'face': {'lid': 0.85, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': -0.2, 'puff': 0.5}}, toonDur=0.0),
         k(BITE1, toon={**HAND(GRIP1(MOUTH1)), 'sq': [1.05, 0.95, 1.05], 'bend': {'neck': [0.24, 0, 0, 1, None]}, 'face': {'lid': 0.9, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': -0.4, 'puff': 0.8}}, toonDur=0.04, toonEase='out'),
         # the tug: the apple goes, the head follows it on a stretched neck, the spine leaning after it
         *[k(r(TUG1 + 0.05 * j), toon={**HAND(GRIP1(AT1(r(TUG1 + 0.05 * j + 0.04)))), 'sq': [r(0.98 - 0.01 * j), r(1.03 + 0.012 * j), r(0.98 - 0.01 * j)],
             'bend': {'spine': [r(0.06 + 0.03 * j), 0, 0, 1, None], 'neck': [r(0.3 + 0.07 * j), r(-0.06 * j), 0, 1, None]}, 'scl': {'head': [0.96, r(1.04 + 0.02 * j), 1.0]},
             'face': {'lid': 0.7, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': r(-0.5 - 0.1 * j), 'puff': 0.4}}, toonDur=0.05) for j in range(4)],
         # the snap: the head flies back with a squash, the eyes spring open
         k(SNAP1, toon={**HAND(GRIP1(AWAY1)), 'sq': [1.14, 0.86, 1.14], 'bend': {'spine': [-0.08, 0, 0, 1, None], 'neck': [-0.22, 0.05, 0, 1, None]}, 'face': {'lid': 0.0, 'eye': 0.45, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': 0.9}}, toonDur=0.03, toonEase='out'),
         k(r(SNAP1 + 0.1), toon={**HAND(GRIP1(AWAY1)), 'sq': [0.96, 1.05, 0.96], 'bend': {'neck': [0.06, 0, 0, 1, None]}, 'face': {'lid': 0.1, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': 0.6, 'gx': -0.6, 'gy': 0.5}}, toonDur=0.06),
         k(r(SNAP1 + 0.08), look=add(AWAY1, [0, 0.05, 0]), lookDur=0.08),
         k(r(SNAP1 + 0.2), toon={**HAND(GRIP1(AWAY1)), 'face': {'lid': 0.2, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': 0.4, 'gx': -0.6, 'gy': 0.5}}, toonDur=0.08),
         *HDT(0.6, add(AWAY1, [0, 0.05, 0]), keep={**HAND(GRIP1(AWAY1)), 'face': {'lid': 0.1, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': 0.5}}, blank=0.14, hold=0.22)]
POMK1 = [k(0.0, visible=True), *MOVES(AM1), k(r(SNAP1 + 0.06), squash=[1.15, 0.85, 1.0], dur=0.35)]
st.shot('S01', 'grassland', setOpts=GSET, look=LOOKG, actors=[act('mec', H1, RY1, 'stand', 'neutral', keys=HERO1)],
        props=[*GARDEN(1), P('pommeEntiere1', 'poWholeApple', pos=MOUTH1, opts={'r': 0.13}, keys=[k(0.0, visible=True), k(BITE1, visible=False)]),
               P('pomme1', 'poApple', pos=MOUTH1, ry=r(yaw(AWAY1, F1) - 25), opts={'r': 0.13, 'dir': [0.15, 0.3, 1.0]}, keys=[k(0.0, visible=False), k(BITE1, visible=True), *MOVES(AM1), k(r(SNAP1 + 0.06), squash=[1.15, 0.85, 1.0], dur=0.35)])],
        cams=[C1])
st.cue('sfx:crunch', 'S01', BITE1, 0.45); st.cue('sfx:stretch', 'S01', TUG1, 0.15); st.cue('sfx:twang', 'S01', SNAP1, 0.3); st.cue('sfx:pop', 'S01', r(SNAP1 + 0.02), 0.2); st.cue('sfx:boing', 'S01', 0.82, 0.12)

