# 3: « Refusé : « des dents », c'est au pluriel. » The counter, front and low: the clerk already holds a big stamp up, it trembles, she slams it on
#    the form (a squash of the stamp and of her); the form springs up to the lens with a big red cross; two hard finger-taps on it, on « dents » and on
#    « pluriel » (the arm winds up high and out, the finger chops down, her head bobs with each, the form jolts back), breathing and a blink between them;
#    then a slow smug head tilt, eyes half shut, a blink (PLURIEL stamps over the top; her head stays under the card band)
